.SH NAME
.PP
auto-web-self-sign - Generate and activate a self-signed certificate

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-web-self-sign web-server [--server-version sv]
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
web-server          Server software (e.g. apache)
--server-version sv Optional server version if not the default
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-web-self-sign
command generates and activates a self-signed certificate for
use with a web server, in order to enable https.

Note that users will be warned about a self-signed certificate
when first connecting.  For a smoother user experience without
warnings, see https://letsencrypt.org/.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-web-self-sign
.ad
.fi

